save(k,t,dict(changes=cs,decisions=ds,inventory=ivs,notes='Manuscript page 5, pencil 10. The source reduces continuity to (15), then proves it under the finite-index condition (16) on the projected stabilizer H_u. The closing cross-reference actually reads (14), then (15), although C had (13). The two arrowheads in (15) and the composed-map diagram are visible in tight crops. The lower marginal note says the right Aut(X)-orbits are already open; it has small lowered signs after the two Aut symbols, the second of which remains doubtful. The source itself supplies the qualification needed for the preceding construction. Its proof uses compactness of the profinite stabilizer and the quotient topology on its projection. The tiny cancelled word before the last equality remains uncertain.',doubts=[['before final equality',r'\deleted{\unsure{on}}','A cancellation obscures the letter sequence.','low'],['second marginal NB, cancelled word',r'\deleted{\unsure{classes}}','The long horizontal cancellation crosses the middle letters.','low'],['second marginal NB, second group',r'\operatorname{Aut}_{\unsure{1}}(Y)','Minute lowered 1 or a terminal stroke; retained without mathematical regularization.','low']],hand=[['Small terminal arrowheads','Both disputed map signs on this page have a dark convergent head; the dash in (16) does not.','C left (15) doubtful and used a dash in the composed map.'],['Small lowered group signs','A closed 0 after the first Aut is visible in the second NB; the second lowered sign remains doubtful.','H omitted both small signs.']],notation=[['H_u','Projection of G_u to Aut(Y); this finite-index condition is explicitly written.'],['=','Used in prose for même.'],['Aut_0(X), Aut_{unsure 1}(Y)','Tiny lowered signs in the marginal note, without a definition on this leaf.']],abbreviations=[['tte','toute'],['top.','topologie'],['automs','automorphismes']],checks=[check('142-011-continuity','(15)–(16)','Finite index of every H_u makes the composition map continuous.','Checked: G_u is compact and its projection to H_u is a quotient map; on it v phi u=vu psi is continuous. On each left coset alpha_i H_u the same argument applies to v alpha_i. A closed finite-index subgroup of a compact group is open, so finitely many open cosets give global continuity. This checks the displayed local argument with the compact profinite topologies already in use.'),check('142-011-open-orbits','second marginal NB','Condition (16) makes each Aut(X)-orbit open in its Aut(X)×Aut(Y)-orbit.','Checked via the quotient of the product group: the Aut(X)-orbit corresponds to H_u in the second factor. H_u is open by the preceding compact finite-index argument; its inverse image is open, so the orbit is open.')]))
